title start
kind: research
tags: business-plan platforms platforms-video-specs
Platforms video specs
title end

section start
title start
Abstract
title end

paragraph start
Question: which video format is shared by TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts. Method: a web search of creator and tool vendor guides, read on 2026-10-29. Result: the guides agree on a 9:16 vertical frame at 1080 by 1920 pixels for all three, while maximum length, file size and safe area values differ between guides. Limit: all sources are secondary vendor guides, official platform help pages were not read, so lengths and sizes are unverified.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Introduction
title end

paragraph start
The brand starts on every platform, so one master format that fits all of them saves work. This page records what the evidence supports.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Methods
title end

paragraph start
Searched the web once for 2026 short video specifications and read the results. Vendor guides were used because no official page appeared in the results.
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Results
title end

paragraph start
Several guides recommend 9:16 at 1080 by 1920 pixels for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts (Sendible, Blitzcut, Frameo, secondary, checked 2026-10-29).
paragraph end

paragraph start
Reported maximum lengths conflict. Shorts are given as up to 3 minutes, Reels as 90 seconds, 3 minutes or 20 minutes depending on the guide, and TikTok as up to 10 minutes. No length is adopted.
paragraph end

paragraph start
A guide states that each platform interface covers part of the frame, so the safe area must be measured per platform (Kapwing, secondary).
paragraph end

paragraph start
One guide reports that YouTube made 9:16 the official Shorts ratio in October 2024 (PostEverywhere, secondary, unverified).
paragraph end

section end

section start
title start
Discussion
title end

paragraph start
Working rule for the plan: shoot and master in 9:16 at 1080 by 1920 with one shared safe margin, and read the length and file size limits on each official upload help page before relying on them.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: read the official upload help page of each platform and record length, size and safe area with the date
Not verified yet.
paragraph end

section end

